							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
		</section>
		<section id="e02349">
			<title>Rear windshield wiper/washer</title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02350">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e02351">
									<figgroup>
										<image href="../../images/OSW035469L.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02352"/>
									</figgroup>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<ol outputclass="callout" id="e02353">
				<li>
					<p>Wiper speed control (front)</p>
					<ul id="e02354">
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">1x</term> – Single wipe</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">O</term> – Off</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">AUTO</term> – Automatic control wipe</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">1</term> – Low wiper speed</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">2</term> – High wiper speed</p>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Auto control wipe time adjustment</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Wash with brief wipes (front)</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Rear wiper/washer control</p>
					<ul id="e02355">
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">2</term> – Continuous wipe</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">1</term> – Intermittent wipe</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p> <term translate="no">O</term> – Off</p>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Wash with brief wipes (rear)</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<note type="note">
				<p>If there is heavy snow or ice on the windshield, defrost the windshield for approximately 10 minutes, or until the snow and ice are removed, before operating the windshield wipers. Operating the wipers and washers without clearing the snow or ice may damage the wiper and washer system.</p>
			</note>
			<note type="tip">
				<p>When driving on snowy roads, the windshield wipers may stop due to snow buildup on the windshield. This is normal and not a malfunction. It is a safety feature designed to prevent vehicle accidents and avoid damage to the wiper motor caused by overloading. If the wipers stop, remove any snow accumulated at the top or bottom of the windshield before operating them again.</p>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
</concept>